<title>RUSSIA: Russian Duma rejects list on output-sharing deposit.</title>
<headline>Russian Duma rejects list on output-sharing deposit.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's State Duma lower house of parliament rejected on Friday in a first reading a list of seven deposit reserves which deputies had proposed should be open to production-sharing agreements.</p>
<p>The list includes oil and gas deposit Prirazlomnoye in the Barents Sea shelf, Romashkinskoye deposit in Tatarstan, a group of deposits on Sakhalin island, Yakovlevskoye ore deposit in Begorod region, Kuranakh group of gold deposits, Samotlor gas condensate in Siberia and Krasnoleninskoye oil deposit.</p>
<p>Earlier chairman of the Duma natural resources committee Alexei Mikhailov told Reuters that only two of the deposits -- Kuranakh group of gold reserves and Prirazlomnoye oil reserve -- would be open to development with foreign companies.</p>
<p>-- Irina Demchenko, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
